{"id":"word:hebrew:H7896","type":"word","title":"שִׁית","subtitle":"H7896 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to place (in a very wide application)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שִׁית (H7896) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 86 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שִׁית (shîyth) means to place (in a very wide application) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 11 34."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שִׁית","transliteration":"shîyth","pronunciation":"sheeth","strong":"H7896","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7896","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יָּ֥שֶׁת","אָשִׁ֥ית","שָׁ֥ת","יָשִׁ֤ית","יָשִׁ֥ית"],"morphs":[["HVqi3ms",9],["HVqi1cs",9],["HC/Vqw3ms",6],["HVqi2ms",6],["HVqp3ms",4],["HVqp3cp",4],["HVqp2ms",3],["HVqi2ms/Sp3mp",3],["HVqp3fs",2],["HC/Vqw2ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to place (in a very wide application)","usage":"apply, appoint, array, bring, consider, lay (up), let alone, × look, make, mark, put (on), regard, set, shew, be stayed, × take.","full":"H7896. shith שִׁית verb put, set (Nö Beitr. z. Semitic Sprachwiss, 39 f. ; compare Phoenician שת Lzb 375 ; Ecclus שית Passive participle Ecclesiasticus 31:27 (?); see also (Nö l.c. 41 ) Syriac quality, appearance ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular שָׁת Gen 4:25 +, 3 feminine singular שָׁ֫תָה 1Sam 4:20 +, 2 masculine singular שַׁ֫תָּה Psa 8:7 שַׁ֫תָּ 90:8 , suffix שַׁתַּ֫נִי 88:7 ; 88:9 , 1 singular שַׁ֫תִּי 73:28 +; 3 plural שָׁ֫תוּ Exod 33:4 3 t., metaplastic יָשִׁית Psa 49:15 ; 73:9 (other forms not found); Imperfect 3masculine singular יָשִׁית Exod 21:22 +, jussive יָשֵׁת Job 9:33 , וַיָּ֫שֶׁת Gen 30:40 +; 3 feminine singular suffix וַתְּשִׁתֵ֫חוּ Ruth 4:16 , תְּשִׁיתֵ֫מוֺ Psa 21:10 +, 1 singular suffix אֲשִׁתֶ֫נּוּ 1Kin 11:34 ; Imperative masculine singular שִׁית Prov 27:23 , שִׁיתָ֫ה Psalm 9:21; Psa 141:3 ; feminine singular שִׁ֫תִי Jer 31:21 , etc.; Infinitive absolute שֹׁת Isa 22:7 ; construct שִׁית Job 30:1 +; Passive participle וְשִׁית ( Jer 13:16 Qr, but read Kt יָשִׁית ); suffix שִׁתִי Exod 10:1 ; &#8212; 1 put, lay hand upon, עַל , Gen 46:4 (E), 48:14 , 17 (J), Job 9:33 ; Psa 139:5 ; with עִם in evil partnership, Exod 23:1 (E); put ornaments, עַל person, 33:4 (J); compare 1Sam 2:8 ; Isa 15:9 ; Job 22:24 ; Ruth 3:15 ; lay child into ( ב ) bosom 4:16 ; put wisdom, ב location, Job 38:36 , compare Prov 26:24 ; בְּנַפְשִׁי עֵצוֺת אָשִׁית Psa 13:3 , i.e. take counsel, plan; בי ׳סַחְסִי 73:28 ; put things רַגְלָיו תַּחַת 8:7 ; lay (penalty) עַל person Exod 21:22 (E), sin Num 12:11 (E), compare (with אֲשֶׁר = where ) Psa 84:4 ; nearly = give ( נתן ), accusative + ל person Gen 4:25 (J; explanation of name שֵׁת ), appoint Psalm 9:21. 2. a. set, station , sheep לְבַדּוֺ Gen 30:40 , compare עַל שָׁתָם לֹא 30:40 (J); accusative of person = appoint ( עַל over ) 41:33 (E); set לָמוֺ person ( ל 3b ) + ב location Psa 73:18 , so (accusative) 88:7 and (object person omitted) 12:6 , set crown לְראֹשׁוֺ 21:4 , set one ( מִן partitive) לְכִסֵּא 132:11 ; set person among ( ב person) 2Sam 19:29 ; Jer 3:19 , compare ( עִם ) Job 30:1 ; set watch לְפִי Psa 141:3 , snares לִי 140:6 , enmity, בֵּין person Gen 3:15 (J); iniquities לְנֶגְדֶּ֑ךָ Psa 90:8 , compare 101:3 ; set, direct face, אֶל location Num 24:1 (J), eyes בָּאָרָץ לִנְטוֺת Psa 17:11 . b. in phrase ׳שׁ לְ לֵב set one's mind to , give heed, attention (compare שׂוּם 2b ), Exod 7:23 (E), 2Sam 13:20 ; Jer 31:21 ; Psa 48:14 ; Prov 22:17 ; 27:23 , with אֶל Job 7:17 , absolute 1Sam 4:20 ; Psa 62:11 ; Prov 24:32 I reflected . c. set, fix , נְּבוּל Exod 23:31 (E; with עַד ֗֗֗ מִן ), חֹק לִי תָּשִׁית Job 14:13 wouldst fix me a limit, 38:11 ( גַּלָּיךָ בִּגְאוֺן יָשִׁית וּפאֹ De and others here shall one fix it [the boundary, חֹק , 38:10 ] = it shall be fixed against, etc.: but explanation very forced: Me Kau ג ׳יִשָּׁבֵר , Bi Bu ג ׳יִשְׁבֹּת 3 constitute, make one something, 2 accusative, 1Kin 11:34 I will make him prince , Isa 5:6 ; 26:1 ; Jer 22:6 ; Psa 21:7 ; 84:7 ; 88:9 ( + למוֺ indirect object), 110:1 ; 2Sam 22:12 || Psa 18:12 ; שֶׁ֑כֶם תְּשִׁיתֵמוֺ 21:13 = thou wilt make them (all) shoulder , make them turn their back, flee (compare 18:41 ); accusative + ל make something into Jer 2:15 = 50:3 ; 13:16 ; Psa 45:17 ( + ב location); accusative + כ compare make one like Hosea 2:5 (|| שִׂים ), Isa 16:3 ; Psa 21:10 ; 83:12 ; 83:14 ; accusative only, make, prepare , feast Jer 51:39 , compare לָח קָצִיר שָׁת Hosea 6:11 (read possibly שִׁית , passive participle), make darkness Psa 104:20 ; = perform signs, ב location Exod 10:1 (J). 4 internally transitive , = take one's stand (compare שִׂים 4a ) הַשָּׁ֑עְרָה שָׁתוּ שֹׁת הַמָּרָשִׁים Isa 22:7 ; with ׳עַליֿ ( against ) Psa 3:7 . &#8212; מִמֶּנִּי יָשִׁית Job 10:20 (Kt; &gt; Qr Imperative וְשִׁית ) is dubious, יָשִׁית = יָשֵׁת : De direct (attention) away from me , compare Di (ellipsis of מָּנִים יָד, , or לֵב ), Du (sc. יָד ; reads Imperative ); Lag (so Bu) proposes יִשְׁבֹּת , Siegf ( יָדוֺ ) ᵐ5 יָוֵב, Beer (best) שְׁעֵה ( 7:19 ), with חֶלְדִּי יְמֵי ( ᵐ5 Bu Be Du) for יחדל יָמַי probably rightly. Hoph`al (or Qal passive Ges § 53u ), Imperfect 3masculine singular יוּשַׁת Exod 21:30 (E) if a ransom be imposed עָלָיו , 21:30 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 11 34","keyReferences":["1Kgs 11 34","1Sam 2 8","1Sam 4 20","2Sam 13 20","2Sam 19 29","2Sam 22 12","Exod 7 23","Exod 10 1"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":86,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 11 34","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲשִׁתֶ֗/נּוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi1cs/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 8","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יָּ֥שֶׁת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 4 20","book":"1Sam","chapter":4,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"שָׁ֥